# Best Practice for Passing Clock to Methods

Here are the verbatim sentences about best practice:

> "Best practice for applications is to pass a `Clock` into any method that requires the current instant. A dependency injection framework is one way to achieve this:"

And regarding testing:

> "This approach allows an alternate clock, such as [`fixed`](../../java/time/Clock.html#fixed-java.time.Instant-java.time.ZoneId-) or [`offset`](../../java/time/Clock.html#offset-java.time.Clock-java.time.Duration-) to be used during testing."

The documentation includes this example code:

```java
public class MyBean {
  private Clock clock;  // dependency inject
  ...
  public void process(LocalDate eventDate) {
